=== ''Eyes of Wakanda'' (2025) ===
{{Main|Eyes of Wakanda{{!}}''Eyes of Wakanda''}}
The [[Hatut Zaraze]], [[Wakanda (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Wakandan]] warriors, carry out dangerous missions around the world to retrieve [[Vibranium (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|vibranium]] artifacts throughout history.<ref name="EoWProjectProfile" />

''Eyes of Wakanda'' was announced from Marvel Studios Animation in December 2023,<ref name="MarvelStudiosAnimationDec2023" /> created in collaboration with ''[[Black Panther (film)|Black Panther]]'' (2018) and ''[[Black Panther: Wakanda Forever]]'' (2022) director [[Ryan Coogler]]'s production company [[Proximity Media]]. In May 2024, Todd Harris was revealed to have created the series,<ref name="HarrisEyesMay2024" /><ref name="HarrisEyesJan2024" /> and he serves as the director and [[showrunner]].<ref name="DisneyJan2025" /><ref name="HarrisEyesConfirm" /> He previously served as a storyboard artist at Marvel Studios.<ref name="HarrisEyesJan2024" /><ref name="HarrisEyesConfirm" /> John Fang also directs.<ref name="EoWDirectors" /> ''Eyes of Wakanda'' was released on August 1, 2025,<ref name="EoWReleaseDate" /> and consist of four episodes.<ref name="TVLineAug2024" />

''Eyes of Wakanda'' is set in several past time periods, with its respective episodes set in 1260 BC [[Crete]] during the [[Bronze Age]], 1200 BC during the [[Trojan War]], 1400 AD China at the start of the [[Ming dynasty]], and 1896 AD Ethiopia during the [[First Italo-Ethiopian War]].<ref name="EoWDirectors" /><ref name="EoWTimeline" /><ref name="EoWTimelinePoster" />

=== ''Marvel Zombies'' season 1 and ''The Winter Soldier'' special (2025–present) ===
[[File:Zeb Wells by Gage Skidmore 2 (cropped).jpg|thumb|upright=0.75|[[Zeb Wells]], the head writer of ''Marvel Zombies''|alt=Zeb Wells at Comic-Con in 2023]]
{{Main|Marvel Zombies (TV series){{!}}''Marvel Zombies'' (TV series)}}
A group of survivors fight against former heroes and villains that have been turned into zombies.<ref name="SDCC2022CBR" />

In November 2021, an animated series based on the comic book series ''[[Marvel Zombies (comic book)|Marvel Zombies]]'' was announced,<ref name="MarvelZombiesVariety" /><ref name="Disney+DayDeadline" /> with [[Bryan Andrews (filmmaker)|Bryan Andrews]] directing and [[Zeb Wells]] serving as [[head writer]];<ref name="MarvelZombiesVariety" /> Andrews was later revealed as showrunner.<ref name="DisneyJan2025" /><ref name="ZombiesReleaseDate" /> It is a continuation of the reality first introduced in the ''[[What If...? (TV series)|What If...?]]'' episode "[[What If... Zombies?!]]" and includes characters introduced in [[Marvel Cinematic Universe: Phase Four|Phase Four]] of the MCU.<ref name="MarvelZombiesContinuation" /> ''Marvel Zombies'' was released on Disney+ on September 24, 2025, and consists of four episodes.<ref name="ZombiesReleaseDate" /> In January 2026, active development on a continuation of ''Marvel Zombies'' had begun with Andrews,<ref name="WinderbaumJan2026Continuation" /> and had entered production by April 2026.<ref name="WinderbaumS2Animatics" /> That October, the two-episode special, ''The Winter Soldier'', was announced,<ref name="NYCC2026Marvel" /> with Jennifer Muro producing and serving as [[head writer]] on the special.<ref name="Muro" /> ''The Winter Soldier'' will be released in October 2027. Two additional specials, ''The Fist of Khonshu'' and ''The Last Guardian'', will be released in 2028 and 2029, respectively.<ref name="NYCC2026Marvel" />

The first season of ''Marvel Zombies'' is set in 2023, five years after the events of the ''What If...?'' episode.<ref name="ZombiesTimeline" /> Over 15 actors reprise their MCU roles in the season, with several actors from ''What If...?'' also reprising their roles.<ref name="MarvelZombiesCast" /> [[Todd Williams (actor)|Todd Williams]] voices [[Blade (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Eric Brooks / Blade Knight]] in the series.<ref name="WilliamsZombies" /><ref name="ZombiesReleaseDate" />

=== ''Wonder Man'' (2026) ===
{{Main|Wonder Man (TV series){{!}}''Wonder Man'' (TV series)}}
[[File:Destin Daniel Cretton by Gage Skidmore (cropped 2).jpg|thumb|upright=0.75|left|[[Destin Daniel Cretton]], director of ''Spider-Man: Brand New Day'' and co-developer of ''Wonder Man''|alt=Destin Daniel Cretton speaking into a microphone at Comic-Con in 2019]]
Struggling actor [[Simon Williams (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Simon Williams]] and actor [[Trevor Slattery]] try to earn roles in the remake of the superhero film ''Wonder Man''.<ref name="WonderManProjectProfile" />

In December 2021, Destin Daniel Cretton signed a multi-year deal with Marvel Studios to develop television projects for Disney+, with a comedy series already in development by then, through Cretton's company [[Family Owned (company)|Family Owned]].<ref name="ShangChiSequelConfirmed" /><ref name="ShangChiSequelVariety" /> In June 2022, the series was revealed to be ''Wonder Man'', centered on the character [[Wonder Man|Simon Williams / Wonder Man]], with [[Andrew Guest]] joining to develop the series and serve as head writer;<ref name="WonderManSeries" /> Guest later became [[showrunner]].<ref name="KangDynastyCrettonExit" /> In October, [[Yahya Abdul-Mateen II]] was cast as the title character.<ref name="Abdul-MateenWM" /> Filming began in April 2023 in Los Angeles,<ref name="WonderManFilming" /><ref name="WonderManRadford" /> with Cretton, [[James Ponsoldt]], Tiffany Johnson, and [[Stella Meghie]] directing episodes of the series,<ref name="WonderManDirectors" /> but was shut down the next month because of the WGA strike.<ref name="WonderManStrikeImpact" /> Filming resumed in January 2024,<ref name="WonderManFilmingResume" /> and concluded by that April.<ref name="WMApr2024" /> The first season of ''Wonder Man'' was released in its entirety on Disney+ on January 27, 2026,<ref name="WMReleaseDate" /> as part of the "[[Marvel Spotlight (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Marvel Spotlight]]" banner,<ref name="KangDynastyCrettonExit" /> and consists of eight episodes.<ref name="WonderManEps" /> The series was renewed for a second season in March 2026,<ref name="WonderManS2Renewal" /> but was canceled that July.<ref name="WonderManS2Canceled" />

''Wonder Man'' spans multiple years, from around late 2025 until 2027.<ref name="WMTimeline" /> [[Ben Kingsley]] and [[Arian Moayed]] reprise their respective MCU roles of [[Trevor Slattery]] and [[Department of Damage Control]] agent [[P. Cleary]].<ref name="KingsleyWM" /><ref name="MoayedWM" />

=== ''Daredevil: Born Again'' seasons 2 and 3 (2026–present) ===
{{Main|Daredevil: Born Again{{!}}''Daredevil: Born Again''|Daredevil: Born Again season 2{{!}}''Daredevil: Born Again'' season 2|Daredevil: Born Again season 3{{!}}''Daredevil: Born Again'' season 3}}
In the second season, New York City mayor [[Wilson Fisk (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Wilson Fisk / Kingpin]] and his [[Anti-Vigilante Task Force]] (AVTF) are hunting [[Matt Murdock (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Matt Murdock / Daredevil]] after Fisk's consolidation of power. Murdock goes underground and gathers allies to resist Fisk's corruption and the AVTF.<ref name="DDBAS2Premise" /><ref name="DisneyUpfronts2025THR" />

The [[Daredevil: Born Again season 1|first season]] of ''Daredevil: Born Again'' premiered in March 2025.<ref name="DDBAEWFeb2025" /> The series was announced in July 2022 with an 18-episode first season,<ref name="SDCC2022" /> but following its creative overhaul in September 2023, this was split into two seasons,<ref name="DDBATVLineFeb2025" /><ref name="DDBAEWFeb2025" /> and the series was renewed for a third and final season in September 2025.<ref name="DDBAS3Confirmed" /><ref name="DDBAS3Final" /> [[Charlie Cox]] and [[Vincent D'Onofrio]] return to star as Murdock and Fisk, respectively,<ref name="DDBAS2Filming" /><ref name="DDBAS3Filming" /> along with showrunner [[Dario Scardapane]].<ref name="DDBAS2Scardapane" /><ref name="DDBAS3Scardapane" /> Scardapane left the series in September 2026 after his contract was not renewed by Marvel in the midst of the third season's post-production.<ref name="DDBAS3Final" /> Directors [[Justin Benson and Aaron Moorhead]] returned for the second and third seasons,<ref name="DDBAS2EpisodeCount" /><ref name="DDBAS3BensonMoorhead" />{{independent source needed|date=March 2026}} with [[Iain B. MacDonald]] and [[Solvan Naim|Solvan "Slick" Naim]] also directing in both seasons,<ref name="DDBAS2ProjectProfile" /><ref name="MacDonaldDDBAS3" /><ref name="SlickNaimClapperboard" /> while Angela Barnes served as a director in the second,<ref name="DDBAS2ProjectProfile" /><ref name="DDBAS2FilmingWrap" /> and Jet Wilkinson served as a director in the third.<ref name="WilkinsonDDBA" /> Scardapane described the second season as the second part of the first season.<ref name="DDBAEWFeb2025" /> Filming for the second season took place from the end of February to July 2025.<ref name="DDBAS2EpisodeCount" /><ref name="DDBAS2FilmingWrap" /> with filming for the third season starting in March 2026 and concluding that July.<ref name="DDBAS3FilmingStart" /><ref name="ColterJonesRitterDDBAS3" /><ref name="DDBAS3FilmingWrap" /> The second season premiered on Disney+ on March 24, 2026, and consists of eight episodes, releasing weekly until May 5, 2026,<ref name="DDBAS2ReleaseSchedule" /> while the third season, also consisting of eight episodes,<ref name="DDBAS3Eps" /> is set to premiere in March 2027.<ref name="DDBAS3Release" />

The second season is set six months after the first season,<ref name="DDBAS2Timeline" /> and is concurrent with the events of ''[[The Punisher: One Last Kill]]'' (2026),<ref name="EWDec2025DDBAS2Preview" /> while the third season is set six months after the events of the second.<ref name="DDBAS3Timeline" /> For the second season, [[Krysten Ritter]], [[Toby Leonard Moore]], [[Royce Johnson]], [[Geoffrey Cantor (actor)|Geoffrey Cantor]], and [[Mike Colter]] reprise their respective roles as [[Jessica Jones (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Jessica Jones]],<ref name="DisneyUpfronts2025THR" /> [[James Wesley (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|James Wesley]], [[Brett Mahoney (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Brett Mahoney]],<ref name="MooreJohnsonDDBAS2" /> [[Mitchell Ellison]],<ref name="CantorDDBAS2" /> and [[Luke Cage (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Luke Cage]] from [[Marvel's Netflix television series]]. In the third season, Ritter and Colter once again reprise their roles,<ref name="ColterJonesRitterDDBAS3" /> and are joined by [[Finn Jones]] and [[Élodie Yung]] reprising their Netflix series' roles as [[Danny Rand (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Danny Rand / Iron Fist]] and [[Elektra Natchios (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Elektra Natchios]].<ref name="ColterJonesRitterDDBAS3" /><ref name="YungDDBAS3" />

=== ''VisionQuest'' (2026) ===
{{Main|VisionQuest{{!}}''VisionQuest''}}
[[File:Terry Matalas Photo Op GalaxyCon Austin 2023.jpg|thumb|upright=0.75|[[Terry Matalas]] redeveloped ''VisionQuest'' as its showrunner and lead director.]]
After being resurrected in ''WandaVision'', the [[synthezoid]] [[Vision (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Vision]] lives in hiding while he attempts to understand who he is by communicating with various [[artificial intelligence]]s (AIs) personas that are embedded in his programming. When a bounty is placed on Vision's head, he goes on the run with a mysterious teenager who may be his reincarnated son.<ref name="VisionQuestTrailer" />

A spin-off series from ''WandaVision'' centered on [[Paul Bettany]]'s character Vision, titled ''Vision Quest'', was in development by October 2022. [[Jac Schaeffer]] was set to return as head writer with Bettany starring,<ref name="VisionQuest" /> but Schaeffer was no longer developing it by May 2024 due to her focus on the first spin-off, ''[[Agatha All Along]]'' (2024), and [[Terry Matalas]] was hired to redevelop the series as its showrunner.<ref name="MatalasVision" /> The series concludes a trilogy that also includes ''WandaVision'' and ''Agatha All Along''.<ref name="VisionNYCC2025" /> Filming had begun by March 2025 at Pinewood Studios in London,<ref name="VisionQuestFilming" /> with Matalas, Christopher J. Byrne, [[Vincenzo Natali]], and Gandja Monteiro directing episodes of the series,<ref name="VQDirectors" /> and concluded in July 2025.<ref name="VQFilmingWrap" /> ''VisionQuest'' premiered on Disney+ on October 13, 2026,<ref name="VQReleaseSchedule" /> and consisted of eight episodes,<ref name="VQEpCount" /> concluding on November 10.<ref name="VQReleaseSchedule" />

''VisionQuest'' is set approximately 18 months after ''Agatha All Along'';<ref name="VisionQuestTimeline2" /> this is years after the events of ''WandaVision'' and around the events of ''Brand New Day''.<ref name="VisionQuestTimeline" /> Various AIs that have previously appeared in the MCU are featured in ''VisionQuest'', including [[Ultron (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Ultron]] (portrayed by [[James Spader]]), [[E.D.I.T.H.]] ([[Emily Hampshire]]), [[F.R.I.D.A.Y. (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|F.R.I.D.A.Y.]] ([[Orla Brady]]), and [[J.A.R.V.I.S.]] ([[James D'Arcy]]);<ref name="VisionNYCC2025" /> in prior MCU media, the latter three AIs were respectively voiced by Dawn Michelle King, [[Kerry Condon]], and Bettany, while D'Arcy played J.A.R.V.I.S.'s human inspiration, [[Edwin Jarvis (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Edwin Jarvis]].<ref name="VQAIActors" /> [[Faran Tahir]] also reprises his role as the [[Ten Rings (organization)|Ten Rings]] leader [[Raza (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Raza]] from the MCU film ''[[Iron Man (2008 film)|Iron Man]]'' (2008),<ref name="TahirVision" /> while [[Ruaridh Mollica]] portrays Vision's son [[Tommy Maximoff (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Tommy Maximoff]] and [[Thomas Shepherd (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Thomas Shepherd]], taking over from [[Jett Klyne]] who portrayed Tommy in ''WandaVision'' and the MCU film ''[[Doctor Strange in the Multiverse of Madness]]'' (2022).<ref name="MollicaTommyVQ" /> Bettany also portrayed [[J.I.M.|J.I.M. / Synthetic Man]], the world's first synthezoid, and J.I.M.'s creator, [[Phineas Horton (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Phineas Horton]], in the series.<ref name="BettanyVQRoles" /> [[Joe Locke]] reprises his role as [[Billy Maximoff (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Billy Maximoff]] from ''Agatha All Along'', while Robert Downey Jr. and [[Elizabeth Olsen]] make cameo appearances in a mid-credits scene in the final episode in their MCU roles of Victor von Doom / Doctor Doom and [[Wanda Maximoff (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Wanda Maximoff / Scarlet Witch]], respectively.<ref name="VQPostCredits" />

=== ''Your Friendly Neighborhood Spider-Man'' season 2 ===
{{Main|Your Friendly Neighborhood Spider-Man{{!}}''Your Friendly Neighborhood Spider-Man''|Your Friendly Neighborhood Spider-Man season 2{{!}}''Your Friendly Neighborhood Spider-Man'' season 2}}
The first season of ''Your Friendly Neighborhood Spider-Man'' premiered in January 2025.<ref name="Oct2024ReleaseDates" /> A second season, initially titled ''Spider-Man: Sophomore Year'', was announced in July 2022,<ref name="SDCC2022AnimationVariety" /> continuing the naming convention of the series' original title, ''Spider-Man: Freshman Year''.<ref name="MarvelStudiosAnimationDec2023" /> Jeff Trammell returned as head writer and showrunner from the first season, and said in January 2025 that the series was not limited to covering one school year per season.<ref name="YFNSMSeasonSchoolYears" /><ref name="TrammellShowrunner" /> The second season is scheduled to premiere on January 13, 2027.<ref name="YFNSMS2Premiere" /> A third season is also in production.<ref name="YFNSMS3" />

