=== ''The Punisher: One Last Kill'' (2026) ===
[[File:Jon Bernthal (53983124020).jpg|thumb|upright=0.75|alt=Jon Bernthal at GalaxyCon Raleigh in 2024|[[Jon Bernthal]], the star, co-writer, and an executive producer of ''The Punisher: One Last Kill'']]
{{Main|The Punisher: One Last Kill{{!}}''The Punisher: One Last Kill''}}
After avenging his family's deaths, Frank Castle searches for meaning beyond revenge while haunted by ghosts of his past, until he is drawn back into conflict by crime lord [[Ma Gnucci (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Ma Gnucci]].<ref name="WollPunisherOLK" />

In February 2025, a [[Marvel's Special Presentations|Special Presentation]] centered on Jon Bernthal's character Frank Castle / Punisher from Marvel's Netflix series and ''Daredevil: Born Again'' was announced to be in development.<ref name="PunisherSpecialSHH" /> [[Reinaldo Marcus Green]] was set to direct the special and was writing the script with Bernthal, after they worked together on the miniseries ''[[We Own This City]]'' (2022).<ref name="PunisherSpecialEW" /> Filming began in mid-July 2025, in New York City,<ref name="PunisherSpecialFilmingStart" /><ref name="PunisherSpecialFilmingStart2" /> and wrapped in early August.<ref name="PunisherFilmingWrap" /> In March 2026, the special was titled ''The Punisher: One Last Kill''. It was released on Disney+ on May 12, 2026, one week after the ''Born Again'' season 2 finale.<ref name="PunisherSpecialRelease" /> It is marketed as a "Marvel Television Special Presentation".<ref name="PunisherMarvelTVSP" />

''One Last Kill'' takes place concurrently with the events of ''Born Again'' season 2.<ref name="EWDec2025DDBAS2Preview" /> [[Jason R. Moore]] and [[Kelli Barrett]] reprise their respective roles from Marvel's Netflix series ''[[The Punisher (TV series)|The Punisher]]'' (2017–2019) as [[Curtis Hoyle (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Curtis Hoyle]] and [[Maria Castle (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Maria Castle]],<ref name="MoorePunisherSpecial" /><ref name="PunisherOLKCastleFamily" /> while [[Deborah Ann Woll]] reprises her MCU role as [[Karen Page (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Karen Page]].<ref name="WollPunisherOLK" /> Bernthal's daughter Addie and Eduardo Campirano respectively portray Castle's deceased children [[Lisa Castle (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Lisa]] and [[Frank Castle Jr. (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Frank Jr.]],<ref name="PunisherOLKCastleFamily" /><ref name="LisaFrankJrRecast" /> replacing [[Nicolette Pierini]] and Aidan Pierce Brennan from ''The Punisher''.<ref name="Pierini" /><ref name="LisaFrankJrRecast" />
